quran[22]{c,v,t}:
  54,50,And Our command comes into action once and for all as the twinkling of an eye.
  54,51,"And surely, We destroyed (many of) your groups. So is there anyone who will take advice?"
  54,52,And whatever they did is (recorded) in (their) Books of Deeds.
  54,53,"And every (action), small or big, has been written."
  54,54,"Indeed, the Godfearing will (rejoice) in gardens and streams,"
  54,55,And will (be seated) in special nearness to the Sovereign Lord of (true) power during holy sessions.
  55,1,"The Most Compassionate (is He),"
  55,2,Who (Himself) taught the Qur’an (to the Arab Messenger [blessings and peace be upon him] or the humans through him).*
  55,3,He is the One Who created humankind.
  55,4,He alone taught him the art of expression and communication.
  55,5,The sun and the moon are rotating according to the configuration determined (by Him).
  55,6,"And the herbs spread over the earth, and all (species of) the trees prostrate themselves (to Him alone)."
  55,7,"And He is the One Who has maintained the sky raised high and (He is the One) Who has set up the balance (for justice),"
  55,8,So that you violate not the balance whilst weighing.
  55,9,And keep weighing justly and do not make the balance fall short.
  55,10,He is the One Who has spread out the earth for the creatures.
  55,11,"There are fruits in it and blossom-bearing date-palms,"
  55,12,And chaff-covered grain and fragrant (fruits and) blooms.
  55,13,"So, (O assembly of jinn and men,) which of your Lord’s blessings will you deny?"
  55,14,"He is the One Who created man from a dry mud sounding like earthenware,"
  55,15,And created the jinn from a flame of fire.
  55,16,So which of your Lord’s blessings will you both deny?
